        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Common Errors\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### One-Dimensional `X`\n",
        "\n",
        "The most common error is passing a one-dimensional predictor array to `sklearn`.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Bad | Good |\n",
        "|------|------|\n",
        "| `x = np.array([1, 2, 3, 4])`<br>`model.fit(x, y)` | `X = x.reshape(-1, 1)`<br>`model.fit(X, y)` |\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Class Name versus Model Object\n",
        "\n",
        "Another common mistake is confusing an `sklearn` class with an object created from that class.\n",
        "\n",
        "For example, `DecisionTreeClassifier` is the class itself.\n",
        "\n",
        "| Bad | Good |\n",
        "|------|------|\n",
        "| `model = DecisionTreeClassifier`<br>`model.fit(X_train, y_train)` | `model = DecisionTreeClassifier()`<br>`model.fit(X_train, y_train)` |\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Mixing Lists and Arrays\n",
        "\n",
        "Use arrays for elementwise numerical operations."
      ],
      "id": "fbefba14"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "[1, 2, 3] * 2"
      ],
      "id": "528efbd7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Plain lists do not always behave like numerical vectors.\n"
      ],
      "id": "53ee75e4"
    }
